ool  i would join the improv club and i was  in the theater club and so um improv  gave me an opportunity to  speak because i spent a lot of my time  silencing myself i was like super  bullied at one point so i would just  like be the quiet kid in the classroom  um just to not bring attention to myself  and it wasn't until like i was able to  go on stage that i was allowed to  not say everything that i wanted to say  but like live freely and so because  improv was like my home away from home i  think comedy does come a little  naturally but then also too angie is  literally my grandma angelia is my  grandma and she's my cousin and she's my  auntie  so that woman i just i know her  you know oh  i love to hear that and that perfectly  leads to my next question which is for  grace grace the character of quinn did  you find a lot of yourself in it or  maybe a grandma grandpa what did you  find in quinn  i'm not gonna lie to you as i was  reading this the script and i was  looking at quinn i was thinking to  myself i don't really connect to quinn  like that you know what i mean like i  just feel like  like i'm i'm more hip to things i'm not  as naive like you know what i mean so i  i wasn't  i wasn't really feeling the quinn vibe  at first and as soon as i got to the  chemistry and i started reading it quinn  and i just aligned and as the show went  on i said i don't know what i was  thinking there is so much of me that's  in quinn so much of quinn that's in me  we're definitely not the same person  there's definitely decisions that we  would have made differently but it  helped me to understand more of where  she was coming from and really operate  from a place of truth and honesty and  like deep down i am obsessed with her i  love her so much like i just hug her  every time i'm i'm you know  speaking for her and and being a vessel  for her i just i hug her deep down  inside because i i feel like there's so  much more that is congruent with me and  quinn than i ever ever thought possible  yeah that's a great answer and it shows  how smart both of you are and how great  it appears on the screen with your  characters you really bring them to life  watch grace and shaniqua kill it all 10  episodes that's the whole season of  harlem is on prime video this friday so  you can fidget this weekend thank you so  much for joining me today guys i hope to  talk to you in the future  thank you so much to you

